        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": " This beautifully maintained five-bedroom semi-detached home occupies a superb position on the Green Road, Mullingar, within a mature and established residential setting just minutes from the town centre. Presented in excellent condition throughout, the property offers generous accommodation together with a large mature rear garden, making it an ideal choice for families or first-time buyers seeking space in an exceptionally convenient location.\n\nThe accommodation opens with a welcoming entrance hall with tiled flooring. The living room features laminate flooring, an inset solid fuel stove and front and rear aspects. The fitted kitchen is finished with tiled flooring and splashbacks and incorporates an integrated oven, electric hob and extractor fan. The generous dining area, which provides excellent additional storage and features a second solid fuel stove with back boiler. A separate utility room offers further fitted storage. A ground floor bedroom, a bright room overlooking the rear garden and a guest WC with an electric shower completes the ground-floor accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, there are four further well-proportioned bedrooms. Three are finished with laminate flooring, with fitted storage provided in two, while the particularly spacious fifth bedroom is carpeted. A family shower room and hotpress complete the first floor.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a large and mature rear garden bordered by established hedging, a garden pond and a block-built storage shed. \n\nThere is also a substantial covered fuel storage area incorporating the boiler and providing access between the front and rear of the property.\n\nThe home benefits from oil-fired central heating, with a new boiler installed in 2025, together with the additional benefit of solid fuel heating.\n\nThe Green Road offers an exceptionally convenient Mullingar location, with the town centre, train station, primary and secondary schools, Regional Hospital Mullingar and a wide selection of shops and everyday amenities all within easy reach. Early viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 2.13m x 4m (7' x 13'1\"): \nTiled floor, understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room 2.87m x 6.9m (9'5\" x 22'8\"): \nLaminate flooring, inset solid fuel stove, storage cupboards.\n\nKitchen 1.77m x 2.75m (5'10\" x 9'): \nTiled fitted kitchen, integrated oven and electric hob, extractor fan, tiled splashback.\n\nDining 3.72m x 4.33m (12'2\" x 14'2\") & 1.11m x 1.47m (3'8\" x 4'10\") & 0.92m x 1.59m (3' x 5'3\"): \nTiled, fitted storage units, tiled splashback, solid fuel stove with back boiler.\n\nUtility Room 1.64m x 2.05m (5'5\" x 6'9\"): \nTiled, plumbed for washing machine, storage presses and shelving.\n\nBedroom One 3.26m x 2.73m (10'8\" x 8'11\"): \nLaminate floor, rear aspect.\n\nGuest WC 1.01m x 1.57m (3'4\" x 5'2\"): \nTiled, WC, wash hand basin, Electric shower, tiled wall and floor, wall mirror, shelving.\n\nLanding 1.15m x 2.17m (3'9\" x 7'1\"): \nLaminate floor, carpeted stairs, hotpress.\n\nBathroom 1.67m x 2.09m (5'6\" x 6'10\"): \nWC, wash hand basin, shower, tiled wall and floor, wall mirror.\n\nBedroom Two 2.86m x 2.87m (9'5\" x 9'5\"): \nFront aspect, laminate floor, solid fuel open fire, fitted cupboard.\n\nBedroom Three 2.85m x 3.85m (9'4\" x 12'8\"): \nLaminate floor, rear aspect.\n\nBedroom Four 3.2m x 3.3m (10'6\" x 10'10\"): Laminate floor, fitted storage.\n\nBedroom Five 3.09m x 4.37m (10'2\" x 14'4\"): Carpet floor.\n\nCovered Fuel Storage Area \n2.41m x 3.97m (7'11\" x 13'): \nBoiler, solid fuel storage area, access to front and rear of the house.\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n•Mature hedging\n•Garden pond\n•OFCH\n•Block built storage shed\n•OFCH\n•5 Bed house\n•Close to town centre\n•Ideal starter home\n•Walkin distance to town\n•Mature family estate\n•New boiler 2025\n\nIncluded\n•Fixtures & fittings\n•Blinds\n•Curtains\n•Light fittings\n•Oven\n•Grill\n•Stove\n\nBER \nBER D\nBER No. 119914745\n\n"
